gpt2codex alpha
==============

One package per Debian architecture; identical .deb for Debian 13 and Devuan
Excalibur. GNU screen and git are required. tmux and Codex are not bundled.
Konsole's runtime KPart and SVG/theme support are recommended; QTermWidget
remains available without Konsole. Missing KPart is reported as unavailable,
never silently described as functioning. Libraries used by both built modules
are mandatory shlibs dependencies. No init/service manager is required.

No maintainer scripts, autostart entry, service, cron, migration or registry
modification is supplied. Upgrades/removal leave user state and running servers
alone. Closing the GUI only disconnects its own terminal clients.

See /usr/share/doc/gpt2codex/gui/README.md for GUI behavior and boundaries.
Initial project setup is a separate explicit operator action, never installation.
